107
00:08:36.413 --> 00:08:43.943
Requests before optimisation: ~2,000 per second average at peak, bursts ~7,000 per second.

108
00:08:44.223 --> 00:08:50.005
After edge + client caching: ~3.1 origin requests per search (L3).

109
00:08:50.285 --> 00:08:51.309
Index size:

110
00:08:51.589 --> 00:09:02.682
200k candidates, then ~430k trie nodes; top-5 pointers per node about 24 MB (L1); times languages times cities.

111
00:09:02.962 --> 00:09:10.215
Log volume: ~220k, 500k queries per day to aggregate; tiny for a batch job.

112
00:09:11.565 --> 00:09:23.192
Small data, huge read rate, strict latency: the whole index fits in memory on every serving node, replicated rather than sharded, unless personal or per-store data makes it too big.

