125
00:10:06.497 --> 00:10:08.823
Trie with top-5 precomputed per node.

126
00:10:09.103 --> 00:10:09.849
Build:

127
00:10:10.129 --> 00:10:12.561
1,152 ms.

128
00:10:12.841 --> 00:10:13.823
Extra memory:

129
00:10:14.103 --> 00:10:17.025
24 MB. p50 or keystroke:

130
00:10:17.305 --> 00:10:21.060
0.2 µs. p99 or keystroke:

131
00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:22.791
2.2 µs.

132
00:10:24.141 --> 00:10:34.253
The first keystrokes are the expensive ones for a plain trie: m had 27,162 candidates below it, and everyone types the first letter.

133
00:10:34.533 --> 00:10:42.703
Precomputed top-k moves the ranking to build time: each keystroke is a walk of prefix-length steps plus a read of k pointers.

134
00:10:42.983 --> 00:10:44.925
Memory: k pointers per node.

135
00:10:45.205 --> 00:10:58.965
Reduce it with a radix or compressed trie (merge single-child chains), storing top-k only on nodes with enough traffic, or using an FST (finite-state transducer, as Lucene's completion suggester does).

136
00:11:00.315 --> 00:11:05.136
Updates: rebuild offline and swap atomically, rather than updating counts in place.

137
00:11:05.416 --> 00:11:12.136
Precomputed lists make in-place updates expensive, because a count change can ripple up every ancestor's list.

138
00:11:12.416 --> 00:11:29.973
Alternatives: search-engine completion suggesters (FST-based) and edge n-gram indexes (Ch 22), sorted arrays with binary search for prefix ranges, or Redis sorted sets per prefix (ZREVRANGE on ac:am) for small, frequently updated sets.

139
00:11:31.323 --> 00:11:32.710
The offline pipeline.

140
00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:40.371
Collect search logs: the query typed, the query submitted, whether the search returned results, what was clicked or added to cart.

141
00:11:40.651 --> 00:11:56.075
Normalise: lowercase, trim, collapse whitespace, unify scripts and transliterations (doodh ↔ दूध ↔ milk as aliases, Ch 22), strip quantities if you want generic suggestions.

142
00:11:56.355 --> 00:12:07.342
Filter: minimum count and distinct users (so one person can't create a suggestion), a blocklist, PII patterns (phone numbers, emails), and zero-result queries.

143
00:12:07.622 --> 00:12:11.675
Suggesting a query that returns nothing is worse than no suggestion.

144
00:12:13.025 --> 00:12:26.401
Score with time decay: each day's count weighted by 0.5^(age or half-life); a trending boost when the last hours exceed the trailing average; a merchandising event calendar for known events.

145
00:12:26.681 --> 00:12:31.076
Quality signals: prefer queries that lead to add-to-cart, not just searches.

146
00:12:31.356 --> 00:12:42.193
Build the trie per language or city, precompute top-k, validate (golden prefixes, size checks, blocklist test), publish a versioned artefact, and let servers hot-swap.

