247
00:18:10.109 --> 00:18:14.055
Keep a per-store unavailable bitmap or re-rank at request time.

248
00:18:14.335 --> 00:18:30.591
Personal history: a small per-user list (last 90 days of searches and purchases, capped at ~200 items), fetched from a key-value store keyed by user and merged at request time: score = global share + w times personal share.

249
00:18:31.941 --> 00:18:42.139
Architecture: global top-k from the trie (fetch k' = 20 to 50 candidates), then re-rank per request with store availability and the user's history.

250
00:18:42.419 --> 00:18:46.237
Personalisation is a re-ranking step, not a per-user index.

251
00:18:46.517 --> 00:18:56.928
Privacy: the user's own history is visible only to them; never mix one user's queries into another's suggestions except through aggregated, thresholded counts.

252
00:18:58.278 --> 00:19:00.262
