267
00:20:40.472 --> 00:20:47.725
The canonical answer is a trie with top-k at each node, built offline from query logs, served from memory, cached.

268
00:20:48.005 --> 00:21:07.803
Stand out by quantifying why subtree search fails on short prefixes, by explaining time decay and trending and their limits (calendars), by making filtering a first-class pipeline stage, by covering client behaviour (sequence numbers, debounce, caching), and by personalising via request-time re-ranking.

